# Story 75: Skill Files (50s)
# Hook: Define an agent once in a file -- name, model, and system prompt -- then spawn it anywhere.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-075-skill-files.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Define an agent once in a file -- name, model, and system prompt -- then spawn it anywhere.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Launch rysh. A skill file is just a markdown file with YAML frontmatter.

[00:08.0 --> 00:16.0]
Let's write one. The frontmatter sets name, description, and model; everything after it becomes the agent's system prompt.

[00:16.0 --> 00:26.0]
Cat the file to see the format: the YAML block between the dashes, then the prompt body. With no frontmatter, the whole file is the prompt and the name comes from the filename.

[00:26.0 --> 00:36.0]
Spawn straight from the file. Double-Escape into rysh mode, then point ##agent spawn at the SKILL.md path.

[00:36.0 --> 00:47.0]
##agent list confirms the agent, built entirely from the file -- reusable, version-controlled, shareable across your team.

[00:47.0 --> 00:50.0]
Skill files turn agents into code you can commit and reuse.

